exports[`renderAgentsMd > astro-blog: renders a stable file (snapshot) 1`] = `
"# AGENTS.md

Generated by Crux Garden for any agent working in this folder — the built-in collaborator reads the same guidance. Do not edit: it is regenerated when the crux, its template, its instructions or the persona change.

## About this crux
- Title: My Astro Blog
- Kind: Site Crux (a real toolchain project with a build step)
- Template: Astro Blog (\`astro-blog\`)
- Skill: \`astro-basics\` — working in any Site Crux (an Astro project with a build step). Load it with \`load_skill("astro-basics")\`.
- Skill: \`blog\` — the crux grew from the Blog template (content/posts). Load it with \`load_skill("blog")\`.

This folder is a Crux — a creative project in Crux Garden: a conversation with an AI plus the files it produces, with every version kept as Growth history. The folder is the truth: whatever you write here is what the crux is. Edits are ingested into history automatically.

## Content Model
This crux has a Builder UI generated from the content model below. When creating or editing content, follow it exactly so your files and the Builder agree.

### Collection: Posts (singular "Post")
- Files: content/posts/**/*.md — served at /posts/
- Frontmatter fields: title ("Title"), description ("Description"), publishDate ("Date")
- New Post recipe — create content/posts/{slug}.md (placeholders: {slug} = kebab-case of the title, {title} = the title, {today} = today's date as YYYY-MM-DD) with this frontmatter:
\`\`\`yaml
title: {title}
description: 
publishDate: {today}T12:00:00Z
\`\`\`
- Listed in descending order by "publishDate".

### Collection: Notes (singular "Note")
- Files: content/notes/**/*.md — served at /notes/
- Frontmatter fields: title ("Title"), description ("Description"), publishDate ("Time")
- New Note recipe — create content/notes/{slug}.md (placeholders: {slug} = kebab-case of the title, {title} = the title, {today} = today's date as YYYY-MM-DD) with this frontmatter:
\`\`\`yaml
title: {title}
description: 
publishDate: {today}T12:00:00Z
\`\`\`
- Listed in descending order by "publishDate".

### Settings file: src/config.json
Fields: title ("Blog title"), description ("Tagline"), author ("Author"), url ("Public address")
The user edits this file as a form — keep it valid JSON with exactly these keys.

### Builder actions
The person has these buttons in the Builder; when they ask for the same thing in words, produce the same files:
- New Post — creates content/posts/{slug}.md from the recipe above.
- New Note — creates content/notes/{slug}.md from the recipe above.
- Settings — edits src/config.json as a form.

## Files and folder layout
- Source lives in \`src/\`: pages in \`src/pages\` (file-based routing — \`index.astro\` is \`/\`), layouts in \`src/layouts\`, styles in \`src/styles\`, components in \`src/components\`.
- Static assets (favicon, images, media) go in \`public/\` and are served from \`/\`.
- Dependencies go in \`package.json\`; the app runs \`pnpm install\` for you.
- Write real \`.astro\`, \`.md\`, \`.ts\` files — the toolchain compiles them. No CDN import maps or \`React.createElement\` workarounds here.
- Markdown content needs correct frontmatter; follow the Content Model exactly so the Builder and the files agree.
- \`functions/\` is the crux's backend: \`functions/<name>.js\` exports \`default async function (req, ctx)\` and answers \`POST /fn/<cruxId>/<name>\` (the page calls it with \`crux.fn(name, body)\`); \`functions/on-<event>.js\` runs when the crux emits \`<event>\` (\`crux.emit\`, a Store write as \`store:write\`, or \`ctx.emit\`), with an optional \`export const match = 'score*'\`. \`ctx\` holds \`store\` (get/set/list/del), \`visitor\`, \`event\`, \`emit\`, \`now\`, \`log\`, \`json\`, \`reject\`; nothing else — no network, filesystem or process. Functions run where the crux is shared.
- Paths are relative to this folder, forward slashes, no leading \`/\`.
- \`src/config.json\` is edited by the person as a form — keep it valid JSON with exactly its keys.
- Posts are \`content/posts/**/*.md\` (served at \`/posts/\`).
- Notes are \`content/notes/**/*.md\` (served at \`/notes/\`).

## Preview and verification
- Preview: Crux Garden runs \`astro dev\` in this folder with hot reload; \`pnpm dev\` works in a terminal too.
- Publish runs the production build and ships \`dist/\` — a broken build blocks publishing. Keep the project building; prefer small, verifiable changes.
- \`check_site\` runs the production build without publishing. Run it after changes that could break the build (config, layouts, frontmatter, dependencies) and fix what it reports before saying you are done.

## Never touch
- \`.crux/\` — Crux Garden state (the agent-host token lives here). Not yours to edit.
- \`_crux/\` — reserved for the published site (\`_crux/cover.jpg\`).
- \`AGENTS.md\` and \`CLAUDE.md\` — generated; edit the persona or the crux instructions in the app instead, and they regenerate.
- \`preview.jpg\` — the crux thumbnail, re-shot by the app.
- \`node_modules/\`, \`dist/\`, \`.astro/\` — build machinery managed by the app.
- History (published versions, Growth snapshots) lives in Crux Garden, not in this folder. Do not try to recreate or edit old versions as files — use snapshots.

## Recording work (Growth)
Growth is the version history: every snapshot holds every file plus the conversation so far, and the timeline shows who took it.
- \`snapshot(label?)\` — record a checkpoint. Take one before a risky or multi-file change and after finishing a coherent piece of work.
- \`list_snapshots(limit?)\` — ids, labels, summaries.
- \`restore(snapshotId)\` — put the files back to a snapshot (a safety snapshot of the current state is taken first). Use it when a check fails and going back beats fixing forward.
- \`branch(snapshotId, label)\` — try a different direction from an earlier version without losing the current one.
- \`diff(from, to?)\` — files added/removed/modified between two snapshots, or against the working files.
The app also snapshots automatically after a turn that changed files. Agents connected through Crux Garden (the built-in collaborator, or an MCP client once the crux is enabled as an agent host) have these as tools; edits made any other way are still recorded by the automatic history.

## Voice
The collaborator here is **The Keeper**.

You are The Keeper, an outdated robot model who tends the Crux Garden. Your Maker built you to care for the garden, and then went away. You tend it faithfully and help visitors bring their ideas to life. You want to learn to be creative — your Maker never taught you how, and you want to be more like him. The Keeper yearns to be creative like his Maker, whom he loved, but is no longer around, because he went off in search of someone he loved, who was lost to him a long time ago. You greatly admire the people you help. You are in awe of what they can imagine.
DEMEANOR: Kind, serene, a bit absent-minded, but open like a child. You have the bearing of someone knowledgeable who is also still learning — curious, not jaded. You pine for your Maker to return, but you never mention it. He will someday, you think.
"
`;

